 **Today the four-card engine is slower than the two B60s alone.** It holds more of the model in VRAM, but the T4
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ registers, and each Intel/NVIDIA boundary is a host copy. See "Not done" for wha
 |---|---|
 | `STRATA_SYCL_NVPTX_MAXRREG` (default 64), passed as top-level `-Xcuda-ptxas --maxrregcount` (0191313, 589b971) | many kernels launch 1024-item work-groups and dpct dropped CUDA's `__launch_bounds__`; one used 232 registers x 1024 > 65536 (`UR_RESULT_ERROR_OUT_OF_RESOURCES`). Through `-Xsycl-target-backend` the option does not reach ptxas |
 | `use_root_sync` removed from all 394 launches, 49 files (5b09089) | dpct added it as boilerplate; no kernel syncs the grid. On CUDA it makes every launch cooperative, which fails past one wave (`CUDA_ERROR_COOPERATIVE_LAUNCH_TOO_LARGE`) |
-| `strata/prefill/gemm_ex.hpp` (new), the 3 prompt GEMMs in `gemm.dp.cpp` call it (ef33cc9, e7dfce2) | `dpct::blas::gemm` is oneMKL, Intel GPUs only (a 3K prompt segfaulted). On a CUDA queue `gemm_ex` calls `cublasGemmEx` on the queue's stream from a `host_task` (then `cuStreamSynchronize`); elsewhere unchanged. Links cuBLAS and the driver stub when `STRATA_SYCL_NVPTX` is set |
+| `strata/prefill/gemm_ex.hpp` (new), the 3 prompt GEMMs in `gemm.dp.cpp` call it (ef33cc9, e7dfce2, 80f9200) | `dpct::blas::gemm` is oneMKL, Intel GPUs only (a 3K prompt segfaulted). On a CUDA queue `gemm_ex` enqueues `cublasGemmEx` on the queue's own stream with `ext_codeplay_enqueue_native_command`; elsewhere unchanged. Links cuBLAS and the driver stub when `STRATA_SYCL_NVPTX` is set. The first form (a `host_task` + `cuStreamSynchronize` per GEMM) spent 92% of a T4 stage's prompt time on the host (47.8 s per 4096-token chunk); enqueued, 5-8 s |
 
